function materialReviewMandatoryValidation_(b,automatic){return '\nMANDATORY VALIDATION BEFORE OUTPUT AND DRIVE UPLOAD\n'+
'1. Supplier names must match their cited excerpts exactly. For every chain_proposals.nodes item, name must appear as an exact, case-sensitive, contiguous substring within that same item excerpt. Preserve spelling, capitalization, punctuation and internal spacing. Do not standardize or expand company names. Example: excerpt "Vendor: ISKRALEGNO S.R.L No: 30294" supports name "ISKRALEGNO S.R.L", but not "ISKRALEGNO S.R.L.".\n'+
'2. Never modify evidence to make a proposed name pass validation. Every excerpt must be copied verbatim from the cited original-page OCR text. Do not add punctuation, correct OCR, join non-contiguous passages or insert a supplier name. Either select a name exactly supported by the excerpt, select another genuine supporting excerpt, or omit the proposal and explain the limitation in summary_vi or the relevant assessment. Preserve original document_id and 1-based page identity; an OCR page is not a paraphrase of that page.\n'+
'3. Validate all proposals and references before saving. Every supplier name must appear verbatim in its own excerpt. Every excerpt must exist verbatim on the specified document_id and original page. Node keys must be unique; KODA is reserved for the final downstream destination, never a proposed node. Every edge endpoint must refer to a proposed node key, except destination KODA. No self edges or cycles. Every edge needs explicit evidence of the stated upstream-to-downstream transaction; names appearing together are insufficient. Omit unsupported edges and explain the limitation. Uncertain section boundaries or grouping require document_type UNKNOWN, empty evidence_block and LOW confidence. Sections must cover every page of every selected PDF exactly once, in order, with unique section_id per PDF. All eight assessment topics must appear exactly once. LEGALITY and DEFORESTATION remain NOT_VERIFIABLE unless authorized independent human verification is explicitly available; this application provides no independent-verification override, so use NOT_VERIFIABLE for both. Every selected PDF must appear once with its exact supplied hash and actual page_count; coverage PARTIAL or UNREADABLE only. Match the supplied schema, identity values, enums and byte limits, with no additional fields, including no system field. Limits: 48000 UTF-8 bytes for the whole JSON, 1–12 summary bullets, 20 proposed nodes, 40 edges, 200 sections total, 300 pages per PDF, 400 characters per chain excerpt, 800 per assessment excerpt. Leave space below the byte limit for application validation metadata.\n'+
'4. Correct failed checks before output or upload. Run these checks programmatically when execution tools are available. Otherwise perform the same checks explicitly. Do not claim compatibility with application rules that were not provided or tested. Do not weaken validation, alter evidence or invent missing references to make the result pass.\n'+
(automatic?'5. Return the final validated JSON only. The application saves and reads back the result; you have no Drive upload tool in this worker. Do not claim it was uploaded or imported.\n':
'5. Save and verify the final validated JSON. This prompt explicitly requests upload to the authorized Drive destination: folder ID '+b.result_folder_id+', exact filename '+b.id+'_MATERIAL_REVIEW.json. Search that exact folder and filename first. If exactly one result file exists, update that same file instead of creating a duplicate. If duplicates already exist, report the ambiguity and do not create another. Read back the saved JSON and verify that it matches the validated output. Report upload success only after verification. If readback fails, report saved but NOT_VERIFIED; if saving fails or authorized upload is unavailable, return the JSON and report NOT_SAVED. Keep any delivery status outside the schema JSON. Distinguish saved to Drive from imported by the EUDR system; never claim successful import without an application acknowledgment. Do not edit source PDFs or Sheets.\n');}

